WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.631
Fifty people, one gymnasium, one day. This is where the context
gets written.

2
00:00:04.911 --> 00:00:11.149
A context is not a platform and not a slogan. It is a description of how the people of this county want their lives to
be.

3
00:00:11.699 --> 00:00:20.497
The first rule is that nobody in the room speaks for a group they do not belong to. The Baptist does not speak for the
Muslim, and the mill owner does not speak for the man who cuts for him.

4
00:00:20.776 --> 00:00:31.328
And the language has a limit built into it. The context cannot say we are a Christian community, or a Jewish community. That
decision was already made by somebody, and it is not theirs to make.

5
00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:42.195
So the line they write is this. All religions are supported and encouraged in our community. Every faith gets the same sentence,
and that is what makes the rest of the document possible.

6
00:00:42.745 --> 00:00:48.659
Then they get to the economy, and here they are specific,
because generalities are how counties get hollowed out.

7
00:00:48.939 --> 00:00:55.417
Liberty County grows timber. That is the backbone of the
economy, and the context says so plainly.

8
00:00:55.697 --> 00:01:02.493
So the question turns practical. How does the county support the industry, and how does it get the best use out of what the woods
produce?

9
00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:07.281
They break it into pieces. Planting, harvesting, and what
happens after.

10
00:01:07.561 --> 00:01:13.319
Planting means a next stand and not a last cut, and it means the
family that owns the land still owns the trees.

11
00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:19.035
Harvesting means mills that stay open, crews that get paid, and
roads that hold up in a wet winter.

12
00:01:19.315 --> 00:01:24.989
And after means the county keeps something. Jobs, a tax base,
and woods that are still woods.

13
00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:35.057
Then the social part. A ball field that is not booked solid. A library that stays open past five. A place to be old and a place
to be young in the same county.

14
00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:42.611
And the spiritual part, which in a timber county is not only
inside a church. It is also in a stand of pines at first light.

15
00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:49.478
Then comes the question that changes the temperature in the
room. What does Liberty County look like in five hundred years?

16
00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:58.473
Not next year, and not the next election. Five hundred years, which is about how long a longleaf pine can stand, and about how
long people have been cutting here.

17
00:01:59.023 --> 00:02:08.298
The picture they described was a mosaic. Ancient groves left standing, mixed in with younger biodiverse forest that gets cut
and replanted in turns.

18
00:02:08.578 --> 00:02:16.167
Clear flowing rivers. Healthy beaver populations, because a
beaver dam is how a river holds water instead of running off.

19
00:02:16.447 --> 00:02:22.125
Wildlife in the forest, and clean air. A county that still makes
its living from the woods without eating them.

20
00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:32.593
That is what a context is for. Every ordinance, every budget, every timber sale gets one question. Does this move us toward
the county we said we wanted, five hundred years out?

21
00:02:32.873 --> 00:02:37.747
If the answer is away from it, the record says so, and anyone in
the county can read it.

22
00:02:38.297 --> 00:02:43.975
Fifty people walked in as strangers with different politics and
walked out with one document about the same place.

23
00:02:44.255 --> 00:02:48.649
It is not a promise that everyone agrees. It is a promise about
the direction.

24
00:02:49.199 --> 00:02:58.156
Video three shows the last step. Putting this on the public record at usaipa dot org, where anyone can read it and track
whether the county keeps its word.
